{"unit_id": "iBobbyTS__dsh-zcode-bridge#readme-1", "repo": "iBobbyTS/dsh-zcode-bridge", "commit": "db6bf137e09dab61a536da4177982199b8449bd3", "type": "readme", "lang": "zh", "text": "@dsh-zcode/bridge README · dsh-zcode-bridge：目标：让dsh接入zcode官方客户端的app server，以实现zcode的agent loop+glm coding plan 150%优惠+可扩展的gui。\n项目已失败，原因：Zcode app-server的bug太多了。遂归档。", "source": "extracted", "section": "dsh-zcode-bridge"}
{"unit_id": "iBobbyTS__dsh-zcode-bridge#readme-2", "repo": "iBobbyTS/dsh-zcode-bridge", "commit": "db6bf137e09dab61a536da4177982199b8449bd3", "type": "readme", "lang": "en", "text": "@dsh-zcode/bridge README · dsh-zcode-bridge：ZCode runs through the official installed Host/app-server and appears in the official\nDSH conversation UI as a registered Agent. The native DSH factory remains available.\nNew sessions default to ZCode; the Hero selects the runtime for the next creation.\nExisting sessions display their locked runtime. The composer model seat forwards\nZCode provider/model/effort choices to the official execution channel.", "source": "extracted", "section": "dsh-zcode-bridge"}
{"unit_id": "iBobbyTS__dsh-zcode-bridge#readme-3", "repo": "iBobbyTS/dsh-zcode-bridge", "commit": "db6bf137e09dab61a536da4177982199b8449bd3", "type": "readme", "lang": "en", "text": "@dsh-zcode/bridge README · dsh-zcode-bridge：Build with `npm ci --ignore-scripts && npm run build`; validate with `npm test`.\nInstall this bundle into an official DSH web profile. Configure the host-backed\nlauncher with its existing isolated launch configuration; credentials remain inside\nthe official process. The plugin starts its connection automatically. An unavailable\nlauncher produces an explicit error instead of creating a native replacement.", "source": "extracted", "section": "dsh-zcode-bridge"}
{"unit_id": "iBobbyTS__dsh-zcode-bridge#readme-4", "repo": "iBobbyTS/dsh-zcode-bridge", "commit": "db6bf137e09dab61a536da4177982199b8449bd3", "type": "readme", "lang": "en", "text": "@dsh-zcode/bridge README · dsh-zcode-bridge：ZCode transcripts and identity bindings are stored under `DSH_HOME/zcode-bridge/`.\nBoot re-registers these Agents. Commands use a bounded authenticated launcher channel;\nlost acknowledgements are queried by their persisted command ID and never resent\nwith a fresh ID automatically. Permission decisions use DSH's approval UI and report\n`assumed-single-answerer`; detecting another client's winning response is unproven.\nThe composer displays “官方 GUI 可能正在运行本会话”. No deletion entry is provided.", "source": "extracted", "section": "dsh-zcode-bridge"}
{"unit_id": "iBobbyTS__dsh-zcode-bridge#readme-5", "repo": "iBobbyTS/dsh-zcode-bridge", "commit": "db6bf137e09dab61a536da4177982199b8449bd3", "type": "readme", "lang": "en", "text": "@dsh-zcode/bridge README · dsh-zcode-bridge：The fork-era conversation/directory bootstrap is retired from the shipped client.\nThe official catalog supplies prefixed ZCode rows. The composer lifecycle dock shows\nthe official queue, steer disposition, active work, stop availability, and distinct\naccepted/queued/rejected/unknown receipts. Queue edit and send-now use official guards;\nthere is no queue removal control. Stop targets the currently confirmed foreground\nexecution. Idle conversation subscriptions release after 30 seconds without a mounted\ncomposer, queued/active work, or unresolved input; the resident transcript stays intact.\nThe carrier supports 64 simultaneous subscriptions and reports explicit capacity errors.\nAfter disconnect, the displayed prefix stays visible, recovery queries original command\nIDs, and a fresh official snapshot supplies the queue and control state. Development fixtures and capability spikes are excluded from publication.", "source": "extracted", "section": "dsh-zcode-bridge"}
{"unit_id": "iBobbyTS__dsh-zcode-bridge#readme-6", "repo": "iBobbyTS/dsh-zcode-bridge", "commit": "db6bf137e09dab61a536da4177982199b8449bd3", "type": "readme", "lang": "en", "text": "@dsh-zcode/bridge README · dsh-zcode-bridge：Only App-owned Electron Host/CLI artifacts are launched. Existing sandbox, HOME,\ncredential, and exact-process ownership restrictions remain in force. The bridge\nnever reads or exports credentials. Shared-GUI arbitration is only proven within\nthis Host; another official GUI process may be running the same session.", "source": "extracted", "section": "dsh-zcode-bridge"}
{"unit_id": "iBobbyTS__dsh-zcode-bridge#readme-7", "repo": "iBobbyTS/dsh-zcode-bridge", "commit": "db6bf137e09dab61a536da4177982199b8449bd3", "type": "readme", "lang": "en", "text": "@dsh-zcode/bridge README · dsh-zcode-bridge：The settings panel adds **Zcode Bridge** to the official `settings.section` and keeps the bridge configuration page in `plugins.bundle.config`. The configuration page exposes the official MCP/plugin/skill catalog, usage/process diagnostics, explicit model connectivity testing, cron/off-peak listings, saved workflows, read-only workspace presentations (official mode and slash commands), and interaction preferences. Session dock panels expose workflow runs and controls, assistant feedback, session-bound v4 attachments, queue preferences, and paused-queue disposition confirmation. Actions show official receipts; reads and reconnects can retry unknown capabilities. No delete, uninstall, or marketplace-removal entry is provided.", "source": "extracted", "section": "dsh-zcode-bridge"}
{"unit_id": "iBobbyTS__dsh-zcode-bridge#readme-8", "repo": "iBobbyTS/dsh-zcode-bridge", "commit": "db6bf137e09dab61a536da4177982199b8449bd3", "type": "readme", "lang": "en", "text": "@dsh-zcode/bridge README · dsh-zcode-bridge：The catalog-sync preference defaults ON and persists in the isolated DSH_HOME. Turning it OFF stops only background incremental sync; startup sync and refresh-before-open still run. The runtime-default note stays read-only (`zcode`). Official interaction preferences use the official GUI's settings-update/runtime-sync flow and apply to the official Host's active workspaces. Connectivity tests and execution controls are explicit actions; opening these panels does not issue model requests. Protocol ownership and approved deferrals are recorded in `docs/protocol-coverage.md`.", "source": "extracted", "section": "dsh-zcode-bridge"}
